    "result_text": "Changing the sheet's today now writes one `SNAPSHOT name=<name> due-total=<due-total>` line per person to the audit file. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec.\n\nThe change is a few lines in `setToday` in `src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/sheet/SheetService.java`:\n- **Due-totals from the day being left:** the method already captured every person's figures before the date changes, for its ROLLUP lines. The SNAPSHOT lines reuse that capture.\n- **List order:** people come out in the order they were added, which is how the screen lists them.\n- **Order in the audit file:** the lines are written before any period closes and before the change's ROLLUP and TOTALS lines.\n- **Formatting:** they go through the app's normal audit service, so a person with no due-total shows `due-total=n/a`. A user acting for a steward by delegation gets ` for=<steward>` at the end of the line, as on other change lines.\n\nI made one judgement call: setting today to the date it already holds writes no SNAPSHOT lines, because the date isn't actually changing. That matches how the existing code only releases claim locks when the date really changes. None of the tests set the same date again, so they don't check this either way.\n\nThere were no front-end or stored-data changes.",
